I don't think this is a duplicate. It seems that the original fix was logically overwritten by https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/pull/34505/changes#diff-7bccf1fcd45159d118d7b2f5f84876d4400217d094e306b5dafba501ba6da65cL75

I found an MCP server with text context only of `use structuredContent` which... open code uses instead of structuredContent. I think the right fix when both are present is to return the structured content along side of the existing content. 

```typescript
if (result.structuredContent === undefined || result.structuredContent === null) return result

return {
  ...result,
  content: [
    ...result.content,
    {
      type: "text" as const,
      text: JSON.stringify(result.structuredContent),
    },
  ],
}
```

Hi @reporter — I hit the exact same bug (GLM-5.2-Coding parent + multimodal subagent on 1.17.20) and traced it down to the source bundle. Sharing root cause + a minimal patch in case it helps the maintainers.

### Root cause

`TaskTool.execute` receives `ctx.messages` (the full parent session, including image `file` parts), but `runTask` builds the child subagent prompt **only** from `params.prompt`:

```js
// runTask, inside TaskTool.execute
const parts6 = await ops.resolvePromptParts(params.prompt);
// ↑ resolvePromptParts only walks text + markdown file references,
//   it never reads ctx.messages, so image parts are dropped here
await ops.prompt({ parts: parts6 });
```

So the image attached to the parent user message is never forwarded into the child subagent prompt, regardless of whether the child model is multimodal. The "model does not support image input" error comes from a *different* downstream issue (see below) — the image never even reaches the child model's `unsupportedParts` check in the first place.

### Minimal patch

Insert image extraction between `resolvePromptParts` and `ops.prompt`:

```js
const parts6 = await ops.resolvePromptParts(params.prompt);
const imageParts = (ctx.messages ?? [])
  .flatMap((m) => m.parts ?? [])
  .filter((p) => p.type === "file" && p.mime?.startsWith("image/"))
  .map((p) => ({ type: "file", mime: p.mime, url: p.url, filename: p.filename }));
if (imageParts.length > 0) parts6.push(...imageParts);
await ops.prompt({ parts: parts6 });
```

### Related secondary bug — `unsupportedParts` modalities format

Even with the patch above, some custom OpenAI-compatible providers (kimi-vision, doubao, MiMo-V2.5) still fail because `unsupportedParts` assumes capabilities are stored as an array:

```js
model.capabilities.modalities.input.includes("image")  // throws if input is an object
```

But providers defined via config get capabilities built as a **boolean object** in the `configProviders` loop:

```js
{ input: { image: true, text: true }, output: { text: true } }
```

So `.includes("image")` throws / returns undefined, the image gets stripped, and the child model never sees it. The `unsupportedParts` check needs to handle both formats:

```js
const input = model.capabilities?.modalities?.input ?? {};
const supportsImage = Array.isArray(input)
  ? input.includes("image")
  : input.image === true;
```

This is also tracked in #30071.

### Verification

Patched both `runTask` and `unsupportedParts` in `app.asar` on 1.17.20 → `@image` subagent (MiMo-V2.5) correctly receives and analyzes attached PNG. Confirmed via server logs that child session now receives `file` parts with `image/png` mime.

Happy to open a PR if maintainers confirm the approach. This is also tracked in #32302 (stalled since June) — both fixes are needed.

补充一下根因分析，与本 issue 标题描述的"`image_url` 未组装"略有不同：

### 实际根因（更上游）

问题不在 `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible` 的格式映射，而在 opencode 的 `TaskTool.runTask` 根本没把图片传给子代理：

```js
// TaskTool.execute → runTask
const parts6 = await ops.resolvePromptParts(params.prompt);
// resolvePromptParts 只解析文本 + markdown 文件引用，
// 不读 ctx.messages，所以父会话消息里的 image parts 在这一步被丢弃
await ops.prompt({ parts: parts6 });
```

`ctx.messages` 里其实有完整的图片 parts（`{type:"file", mime:"image/png", url:"data:..."}`），但 `runTask` 没提取。所以豆包 API 收不到 `image_url` 是因为根本没传到子代理的 prompt，而不是 @ai-sdk 转换出错。

### 最小修复

```js
const parts6 = await ops.resolvePromptParts(params.prompt);
const imageParts = (ctx.messages ?? [])
  .flatMap((m) => m.parts ?? [])
  .filter((p) => p.type === "file" && p.mime?.startsWith("image/"))
  .map((p) => ({ type: "file", mime: p.mime, url: p.url, filename: p.filename }));
if (imageParts.length > 0) parts6.push(...imageParts);
await ops.prompt({ parts: parts6 });
```

### 另一个关联 bug：unsupportedParts 的 modalities 双格式

豆包（以及其他 config 定义的 OpenAI-compatible provider）的 capabilities 在 `configProviders` 循环里被构建为布尔对象格式：

```js
{ input: { image: true, text: true }, output: { text: true } }
```

但 `unsupportedParts` 用 `model.capabilities.modalities.input.includes("image")` 检查，对布尔对象会失败 → 图片被剥离。需要同时处理两种格式（详见我在 #34409 的评论）。

### 验证

在 1.17.20 上同时补丁 `runTask` + `unsupportedParts`，豆包视觉子代理可正常接收并分析 PNG。建议关注 #32302 的合并进度，两个修复缺一不可。

Cross-linking the root cause analysis I posted on #34409 / #36020 / #32302:

The image not being forwarded is because `TaskTool.runTask` builds the child subagent prompt only from `params.prompt` via `resolvePromptParts`, which never reads `ctx.messages`. So the `file` part attached to the parent user message is silently dropped before the subagent is spawned — regardless of Web UI vs CLI, and regardless of whether the parent LLM is multimodal.

Minimal fix (matches #32302, which closes this issue but has been stalled since June):

```js
const parts6 = await ops.resolvePromptParts(params.prompt);
const imageParts = (ctx.messages ?? [])
  .flatMap((m) => m.parts ?? [])
  .filter((p) => p.type === "file" && p.mime?.startsWith("image/"))
  .map((p) => ({ type: "file", mime: p.mime, url: p.url, filename: p.filename }));
if (imageParts.length > 0) parts6.push(...imageParts);
await ops.prompt({ parts: parts6 });
```

A companion fix to `unsupportedParts` is also needed for config-defined OpenAI-compatible providers (doubao, kimi-vision, MiMo) — see #34409 comment for details. Both patches verified working on 1.17.20.
